# Credentials and secrets — never committed, by design (CLAUDE.md rule 3)
#
# NOTE: earlier drafts of this file used broad filename patterns like
# *secret* and *token* to catch credential files. That backfired the moment
# real code existed — "token" and "secret" are legitimate domain terms here
# (OAuth tokens, session tokens, the QBO client secret as a config KEY name,
# not a value) and those patterns silently excluded real source files
# (backend/src/auth/tokenStore.ts, its tests, .env.example, the secret-scan
# script itself). Filename matching is the wrong tool for this anyway —
# gitignore can't see file CONTENTS, so it was only ever a weak, false-
# confidence net. The actual defense against committing a secret VALUE is:
#   - backend/src/logging/redaction.ts + logger.ts (§3.5) — content-scanning
#     at the point secrets could leak into logs
#   - desktop/Scripts/check-no-secrets.sh — content-scanning the desktop
#     bundle for secret-shaped literals, run via `swift test`
#   - actual environment files (.env, not .env.example) never being created
#     with real values inside a path git tracks
#   - manual review of `git status` before every commit — see CLAUDE.md's
#     "Committing changes with git" guidance
# What follows is deliberately narrow: real environment files and specific
# credential file TYPES, not domain words that happen to appear in secrets.

# Real environment files — but NOT the checked-in template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Credential/key file types — these extensions are essentially never
# anything other than an actual secret, so blocking by extension is safe.
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
*.jwt

# QBO / Claude client secrets and OAuth artifacts, by SPECIFIC name — not a
# wildcard on a common word. If you ever export a real secret to a file,
# name it one of these so it's actually excluded.
oauth_client_secret.json
qbo_client_secret.json
claude_api_key.txt

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# --- Swift / Xcode (desktop/) ---
.build/
DerivedData/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
.swiftpm/

# --- Node (backend/) ---
node_modules/
dist/
backend/data/
backend/test/.tmp/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.tsbuildinfo

# NOTE: backend/spike/fixtures/*.json used to be blanket-excluded as
# "runtime state." Reconsidered 2026-08-16: these are the evidentiary
# record every VERIFIED/DISPROVEN status in the capability matrix cites by
# filename — treating them as disposable would mean the matrix's "not
# hand-typed" claim (§12.5) has no artifact backing it. Committed
# selectively instead: keep the small, clean, or otherwise meaningfully
# distinct runs; delete superseded/near-duplicate large ones by hand before
# committing rather than blanket-ignoring the whole directory. Checked for
# secrets before every commit regardless (see the top of this file) — QBO
# response bodies can be large but are not credentials.

# Local scratch
*.local
